.TH SDE-SUITE 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sde-suite, niny, liria, xanara, taca, sde-view, sde-system-monitor, sde-power-manager \- SDE application suite integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-suite
APP [ARGUMENTS...]
.br
.B sde-suite
--list | --check | --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
The native Rust dispatcher integrates distribution-packaged applications into
SDE for DebION GNU/Linux. Niny uses Pluma, Liria uses Caja, Xanara uses Atril,
Taca uses Engrampa, SDE View uses EOM, and the monitor/power tools use MATE.
Arguments are passed without a shell. Liria adds --no-desktop so SDE continues
to own the desktop. These are integration names; upstream application internals,
plugins and licenses retain their original identity.
.PP
Applications follow the SDE light/dark GTK launch preference unless GTK_THEME
is explicitly set or suite.gtk_theme is system. Already running applications
keep their theme until restarted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --check
Report missing suite backends and return nonzero if one is missing.
.TP
.B --list
List suite names, availability, backend programs and source URLs.
.TP
.B APP --source
Print the application's upstream source URL.
.TP
.B APP --copyright
Print the complete installed package copyright notice.
.TP
.B APP --about
Open Settings at the SDE Suite page, including clickable source links.
.TP
.B APP --dry-run [ARGUMENTS...]
Print the backend argument vector without starting it.
.TP
.B sde-power-manager --daemon
Start the MATE power daemon. Normally used by SDE-only XDG autostart.
.TP
.B sde-power-manager --statistics
Open battery/power history instead of preferences.
.TP
.B APP -- [ARGUMENTS...]
Forward arguments directly, including options reserved by the dispatcher.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sde-settings (1),
.BR sde-update (1),
.BR sde-autostart (1)
.PP
/usr/share/doc/sde/SUITE.md and THIRD-PARTY.md contain integration and license details.
